TYPES.md §5.3, §7.2, DECISIONS 460: in expressions every integer is a 64-bit Int, so an integer literal past it is E3201 with no expected type too: a let with no type and an element of a list with none. A declaration with no written type names none.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local let plain = 9223372036854775808

local let many = [1, 9223372036854775809]

local let fits = 9223372036854775807
-- findings.txt --
error[E3201]  a/a.canon:3:19
  9223372036854775808 does not fit Int

error[E3201]  a/a.canon:5:22
  9223372036854775809 does not fit Int

